{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>At every time.</b> It alludes even to the time when Moshe is occupied with receiving the decrees of HaShem and His teachings and the like — these men, being free, would judge at every time, which Moshe himself is unable to do." "<b>And lighten from upon you, and they shall bear.</b> That is, what I am telling you to lighten from upon you is not so that you would not judge at all but only the great matter; rather, <b>and they shall bear with you</b> — meaning, you and they shall be engaged in this task together."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:40.071583296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}